---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@lib/site';
const meta = {
  title: `Editorial policy — ${SITE.name}`,
  description: 'How we select, test, and assess products — and how affiliate links work.',
  path: '/editorial-policy/',
};
---
<BaseLayout meta={meta}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <p>
      This page explains how {SITE.name} chooses and assesses products, and how the affiliate
      links on the site work. If anything here and a review ever disagree, this page wins —
      tell us and we'll fix the review.
    </p>

    <h2>How we select products</h2>
    <p>
      We start from the buyer, not the brand. For a given room size and budget we shortlist the
      units most people are actually choosing between, then narrow by the two factors that
      decide whether a purifier stays switched on: noise on its working setting, and the
      running cost of filters over three years.
    </p>

    <h2>How we assess them</h2>
    <p>
      Where we quote a measurement, we say how it was taken and over what range the comparison
      runs. We do not print star ratings we didn't measure, and we never show a scale bar for a
      number we didn't measure or cite. Specs sourced from a manufacturer are labelled as such.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't print prices. They move, and Amazon restricts where price data may come from. The button is the price check.</li>
      <li>We don't invent review counts, availability, or ratings.</li>
      <li>We don't publish a product card without a genuine drawback. If we didn't find one, we say what we didn't test instead.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      We earn a commission when you buy through our links, at no extra cost to you. As an
      Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases. Commissions never change which
      product we recommend. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">full affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Found a number that's wrong or stale? <a href="/contact/">Email us</a>. Corrections are
      the fastest way to earn a reader's trust, so we take them seriously.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
